From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 22:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] shaders/colorspace: the PQ EOTF of the Dolby Vision decoding
 without cancellation

The Dolby Vision decoding of a signal whose RGB is not BT.2020 (profile 5,
in IPTPQc2, and any RPU that libplacebo-9939 does not take as BT.2020)
goes from L'M'S' to linear LMS by the PQ EOTF, to RGB by a matrix, and
back by the PQ OETF. The EOTF was written as ST 2084 writes it: with
p = N^(1/m2), ((p - c1) / (c2 - c3 * p))^(1/m1). Above a few cd/m^2,
c2 - c3 * p is a difference of numbers close to each other (0.16 against
18.7 at N = 1), and so is p - c1: the relative error of 1e-7 that a float
pow has in p is one of up to 6e-5 in the light (evaluated in float on the
processor between 10 and 10000 cd/m^2: median 1.1e-5, at most 6.3e-5).
The matrix of profile 5 that follows has coefficients up to 3.2 of
opposite signs: in a saturated colour it moves that much of the light of
its bright components into the dark one, and the PQ OETF, steep at 0,
makes hundreds of codes of it. At the edge of BT.2020, a component that
is 0 came out as 0.10 to 0.17 cd/m^2, codes 250 to 315 of 4095, and as
the error changes along a gradient, in bands.

The EOTF is now written with q = 1 - p, computed as -expm1(ln(N) / m2)
by its series, which has the relative precision of ln(N): the numerator
is (1 - c1) - q and the denominator (c2 - c3) + c3 * q, 1 - c1 and
c2 - c3 being 0.1640625 exactly. Where the light is not 0, ln(N) / m2 is
in [ln(c1), 0] = [-0.18, 0], where the series to the seventh power is
exact to 3e-11; below -0.25 the light is 0.

Measured on Mesa's software OpenGL ES (zink on lavapipe) with the Dolby
Vision bridge of Kodi, drawing for output as HDR10 a profile 5 picture
made from a test chart with a real profile 5 RPU (a neutral ramp, the
ColorChecker at 203 and at 1015 cd/m^2, the hues of the edge of BT.2020
up to 1000 cd/m^2), against its reconstruction in double precision (the
composer of ETSI GS CCM 001 and the matrices of the RPU): before, 9.0 %
of the pixels with another 12-bit code, 14634 of them by 16 codes or
more, at most 315 (in 10 bits, 79); now 3.1 %, 15 and 39 (10 bits: 10).
The same with libplacebo 285d1cc, on which the patch applies with -F0 as
well. A picture in BT.2020, which libplacebo-9939 decodes without the
round trip through LMS (profiles 7 and 8.1), gives the same bytes:
measured on 14 pictures of a profile 7 FEL stream, the picture for
output as HDR10, native output in both transports and libplacebo's own
reshaping. On libplacebo v7.387.0, whose PQ EOTF clamps the signal to
[0, 1] as this one does (31f498ec), the patch replaces that EOTF.

License: LGPL-2.1-or-later, that of libplacebo and of the file changed,
whose notice stays as it is.
---
 src/shaders/colorspace.c | 35 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++------
 1 file changed, 29 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/shaders/colorspace.c b/src/shaders/colorspace.c
index a97c2da..27956be 100644
--- a/src/shaders/colorspace.c
+++ b/src/shaders/colorspace.c
@@ -594,12 +594,35 @@ void pl_shader_decode_color_ex(pl_shader sh,
             .data = PL_TRANSPOSE_3X3(dovi_lms2rgb.m),
         });
 
-        // PQ EOTF
-        GLSL("color.rgb = pow(clamp(color.rgb, 0.0, 1.0), vec3(1.0/%f)); \n"
-             "color.rgb = max(color.rgb - vec3(%f), 0.0)            \n"
-             "             / (vec3(%f) - vec3(%f) * color.rgb);     \n"
-             "color.rgb = pow(color.rgb, vec3(1.0/%f));             \n",
-             PQ_M2, PQ_C1, PQ_C2, PQ_C3, PQ_M1);
+        // PQ EOTF, of the signal clamped to its domain, [0, 1] (SMPTE ST
+        // 2084), as upstream clamps it.
+        //
+        // Hades: not in its usual form. With p = N^(1/m2), p - c1 and
+        // c2 - c3 * p are differences of numbers that are close above a
+        // few cd/m^2 (c2 - c3 * p is 0.16 against 18.7 at N = 1), so a
+        // relative error of 1e-7 in p (float, the GPU's pow) is one of up
+        // to 6e-5 in the light. The LMS matrix that follows, of
+        // coefficients up to 3.2 of opposite signs, moves that much of the
+        // bright components of a colour into a dark one, and the PQ OETF,
+        // steep at 0, makes hundreds of codes of it: 0.17 cd/m^2 in a
+        // component that is 0 at the edge of BT.2020 is code 315 of 4095.
+        // Written with q = 1 - p = -expm1(ln(N) / m2), which has the
+        // relative precision of ln(N): the numerator is (1 - c1) - q and
+        // the denominator (c2 - c3) + c3 * q, both 1 - c1 and c2 - c3 being
+        // 0.1640625 exactly. Where the light is not 0, ln(N) / m2 is in
+        // [ln(c1), 0] = [-0.18, 0], where the series of expm1 to the 7th
+        // power is exact to 3e-11; below -0.25 the light is 0 (q = 1).
+        GLSL("{ \n"
+             "vec3 dovi_x = log(max(clamp(color.rgb, 0.0, 1.0), vec3(1e-30))) \n"
+             "              * vec3(%f); \n"
+             "vec3 dovi_q = -dovi_x * (1.0 + dovi_x * (1.0/2.0) * (1.0 + dovi_x * (1.0/3.0) \n"
+             "              * (1.0 + dovi_x * (1.0/4.0) * (1.0 + dovi_x * (1.0/5.0) \n"
+             "              * (1.0 + dovi_x * (1.0/6.0) * (1.0 + dovi_x * (1.0/7.0))))))); \n"
+             "dovi_q = mix(dovi_q, vec3(1.0), lessThan(dovi_x, vec3(-0.25))); \n"
+             "color.rgb = pow(max(vec3(%f) - dovi_q, 0.0) \n"
+             "                / (vec3(%f) + vec3(%f) * dovi_q), vec3(%f)); \n"
+             "} \n",
+             1.0 / PQ_M2, 1.0 - PQ_C1, PQ_C2 - PQ_C3, PQ_C3, 1.0 / PQ_M1);
         // LMS matrix
         GLSL("color.rgb = "$" * color.rgb; \n", mat);
         // PQ OETF
